<title>UK: Iran minister, Iraqi negotiator to London oil conf.</title>
<headline>Iran minister, Iraqi negotiator to London oil conf.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The oil ministers of Iran, Algeria, Indonesia and Egypt and the chief negotiator for Iraq in the recent oil-for-food sale talks at the United Nations have been invited to speak at the 17th Oil and Money Conference in London on October 28-29, the organisers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The International Herald Tribune, which is sponsoring the conference with the Oil Daily Co/PIW Publications, said Iranian Oil Minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh and Abdul Amir al-Anbari, who led Iraq's delegation at the U.N. oil sale talks, were among those invited to speak.</p>
<p>Italian Foreign Minister Lamberto Dini and German Foreign Minister Klaus Kinkel have also been asked to address the conference.</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
